# Docker build context excludes.
#
# The image builds from `COPY . .`, so anything left here is uploaded to the daemon on
# every build and invalidates the layer cache whenever it changes. Without this file the
# context is ~83 MB, of which ~75 MB is .git and bin/ — neither of which the build reads.
#
# IMPORTANT: do not exclude anything the binary embeds at compile time. `go:embed` reads
# from the build context, so excluding an embedded path yields a binary that builds fine
# and then serves nothing at runtime. Currently embedded:
#   internal/web/static          -> the entire web UI (web.SPAHandler)
#   internal/skills/catalog/*.md -> the bundled skills catalog
#   internal/config/default_global_agents.md
# Those must stay in.

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local build output. bin/ alone is ~60 MB and is rebuilt inside the image anyway.
bin/
dist/
*.exe
# Leading slash matters: a bare `relay` would also match cmd/relay/ and silently
# exclude the relay's own source, breaking the build.
/moony
/relay

# Dependency trees that are only needed to regenerate CSS, never to build the relay.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Test artefacts and local scratch.
*.test
coverage.out
*.log
test/browser/test-results/
test/browser/playwright-report/
e2e/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Docs and media: not compiled in, and the media/ PNGs are ~350 KB of pure context.
# (README is kept — it is small and handy for `docker run --rm image cat`-style checks.)
docs/
.github/media/
CHANGELOG.md

# Deployment descriptors describe how to RUN the image; they are never part of it.
deploy/
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
